  "result": "I fixed the ordering in `--help`: an option's names now list the short form first, as in `-a, --alpha`. Before, they came out as `--alpha, -a`. The test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nThe bug was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted an option's names by prefix length from longest to shortest, so `--alpha` landed before `-a`. I removed `reverse=True` from that sort so the shorter prefix comes first.\n\nI read your report as being about the order of names within an option, since that was the only odd ordering I could reproduce. The options themselves already list in declaration order, with `--help` last. If you meant the order of the options in the list, tell me what you expected and I'll look again.\n\nI didn't add a test for this, and I didn't commit the change.",
